 **RL-S1b (`RLS1_ARMS="R0b C1 R1b"`).** The default `RLS1_ARMS` is unchanged (the five original arms); RL-S1b is run by setting the list. Source of truth: `eval/rls1b_arms.json` (`launch_gate.py` profile `refe_rls1b`, which the chain uses for R0b, R1b and, inside an RL-S1b list, C1; `launch_gate.py` was not touched). R0b / R1b are R0 / R1 with `--epo-lam 0.25` and nothing else (`rl_reward.py` and `scorer_finetune.py` untouched); the tests pin the chain's three argv to the JSON token for token and through the REAL gate (`--epo-lam 0.5` is refused). **Order R0b -> C1 -> R1b** (the Master Mind's; the JSON's own `order` field reads C1, R0b, R1b and the chain also accepts that list): R0b is read against C0's banked dumps `/workspace/data/rls1/arms/C0/scores`, which must still be on the pod; R1b is read against C1's. A missing control is a REFUSAL (`RL-S1b arm R0b is read against C0, whose dumps ... are missing`), never a silent fall back to the arm's own arm A. **A K3 kill of R0b (or a K-MON) STOPS the chain**: no C1, no R1b; the chain refuses and the Master Mind decides. The K-MON monitor applies to R0b and R1b. R2b is not registered (it needs a PI decision, `launch_gate.py` `RLS1B_NEEDS_PI`). Insertion points in the script: `RLS1B-INSERTION-POINT-1` (registration), `-2` (`arm_args`), `-3` (the control rule).
 
+**RL-S1c / R0c (`RLS1_ARMS="R0c"`), 2026-10-15. NOT launched: running it is a PI decision (about 3.5 A40-h, beyond RL-S1b's authorised budget, `raw/2026-10-15-rls1-adam-dose/PREREG_R0C_DRAFT.md` section 5).** R0c is R0 with ONE lever, `--epo-ref armA`: the EPO term's KL anchor is arm A's DETACHED policy instead of the frozen base. Source of truth: `eval/rls1c_arms.json` (argv sha256 `f588a6cb...` = R0's banked token argv `24451b62...` with `/arms/R0` -> `/arms/R0c` plus `--epo-ref armA`; `launch_gate.py` profile `refe_rls1c`, which requires the flag NAMED because its parser default `base` would silently reproduce R0). The trainer flag, the profile and the G-DVB entry are `raw/2026-10-15-r0c-build/` PATCH_1..7; the chain wiring is PATCH_8 (`rls1_pod.sh`), tested by `test_rls1_chain.py` and `test_rls1_queue.py` (`--only-rls1c` runs just the R0c arm-loop scenarios and their mutations). **The read rule is the draft's, section 2: "the control for every delta is the arm's own A".** The kill monitor, the kill replay and `rlval_vs_A0.json` (A0 = the base, CTRL = arm A, R = arm B: B - A and B - base) read R0c against ITS OWN arm A, always, even when C0's dumps are on the pod (R0 would be read against them). C0 is the SECOND control: when `arms/C0/scores/scores_update1000_A.npz` exists the chain also writes `rlval_vs_C0.json`; when it does not, it logs `ZZRLS1_R0C_NO_SECOND_CONTROL` and goes on (restore C0's scores from HF `Sayood/tanitad-refe-rls1-c0` and run `rl_val_eval.py` afterwards). R0b / R1b keep their rule (refused when their control is missing).
+*Before the start* (all on the pod, none of it heavy): (1) the landed package, with a SHIP_MANIFEST regenerated at the landing commit (`launch_gate.py ship-manifest --pkg <package root> --commit <40-hex> --out <package root>/SHIP_MANIFEST.json`), is in `/workspace/refe-plan-rls1` - the precheck now also requires `refe/test_rl_s1b.py` and `refe/test_rl_r0c.py` (the gate's suite) and refuses in seconds when they are missing; (2) `ls /workspace/data/rls1/stage/` shows the heavy markers of the earlier runs - `base plan fancmp dbs tlane bank dump_val_s0of1 dump_train_s{0..3}of4 label_val_s0of1 label_train_s{0..3}of4` - a missing one makes the chain REDO that stage (the dump alone is about 3.3 GPU-h); (3) `ls /workspace/data/rls1/arms/C0/scores/scores_update1000_A.npz` for the second control; (4) `HF_TOKEN` (write-scoped) is in the environment of the shell that starts it, never on a command line; (5) no `stage/arm_R0c_killed` from an earlier attempt.
+*The command* (detached, as every RL-S1 start): `RLS1_ARMS="R0c" nohup setsid bash /workspace/refe-plan-rls1/refe/rls1_pod.sh > /workspace/data/rls1/stdout.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &`. Add `RLS1_STOP_AFTER=gate_R0c` for a dry run that does the A40 preflight and mints and verifies the PASS token and stops before the trainer. **What it waits on:** the same QUEUE as every RL-S1 run, so it can be started while the pod is busy. After the cheap precheck (P2 over, the token, the arm names, the files) it holds only `chain.queue` (`ZZRLS1_QUEUED <why>` every 10 min) while ANY chain is ahead: P2, S1 (its `chain.lock`, the S1 H arms), the P2 seed replicate (P2-s1) once past its wait, P6 once past its wait. When nothing is ahead it takes `chain.lock`, settles 20 s and needs the GPU idle on 3 polls; then the finished stages are skipped and the R0c arm runs: preflight -> launch gate (profile `refe_rls1c`, `--arm-name R0c`) -> token verified -> trainer + watcher + kill monitor -> reads -> egress to the private repo `Sayood/tanitad-refe-rls1-r0c` (created by the first push). The pod address is never written into a file.
+*What to look for in `chain.log`:* `arm R0c: preflight PASS, launch gate PASS (token verified)`; `arm R0c: trainer pid/pgid ... (control: .../arms/R0c/scores)` (a control line ending anywhere else is a wiring fault: stop it); `arm R0c: kill monitor READY`; at the end `ZZRLS1_ARM_DONE R0c` and `ZZRLS1_DONE arms: R0c`. A pre-registered kill (K3 / g5 ..., or K-MON) STOPS the chain after the evidence is banked, writes `stage/arm_R0c_killed`, and a re-run refuses until the Master Mind removes that marker or drops the arm. The outcomes, the numbers to read and the next lever for each are `PREREG_R0C_DRAFT.md` section 4 (O1..O5); a separated interval on one training seed is necessary, not sufficient (`H-ESTIM-SEED-1`): the replicate comes before any claim.
